      "jobSummaryDisplay": "<p>Job Title: Certified Medical Assistant</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Location: Morris Cancer Center</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Department Name: OP Cancer Services CINJ</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Req #: 48903</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Status: Hourly</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Shift: Day</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Pay Range: $23.06 - $29.35 per hour</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Pay Transparency:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>The above reflects the anticipated hourly wage range for this position if hired to work in New Jersey.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The compensation offered to the candidate selected for the position will depend on several factors, including the candidate&#39;s educational background, skills and professional experience.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><b>Certified Medical Assistant (CMA) &ndash; RWJBarnabas Health</b></p>\r\n\r\n<p>At RWJBarnabas Health, Certified Medical Assistants become part of a purpose-driven environment where teamwork, compassion, and exceptional patient care create meaningful experiences every day. This CMA role offers opportunities for growth, supportive collaboration, and a culture committed to quality, safety, and continuous improvement. As a Certified Medical Assistant, you will play an essential role in supporting providers, enhancing patient care, and creating a welcoming experience for individuals and families across our organization. Joining RWJBarnabas Health means joining a community where every team member is encouraged to grow, contribute, and make a lasting impact.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><b>A typical day for a Certified Medical Assistant may include:</b><br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>Preparing patients for examinations by obtaining vital signs, documenting medical histories, and ensuring they feel comfortable and informed throughout their visit<br />\r\n\t&nbsp;</li>\r\n\t<li>Assisting physicians and advanced practice providers during examinations and procedures, anticipating clinical needs to support efficient, high-quality care<br />\r\n\t&nbsp;</li>\r\n\t<li>Performing clinical tasks such as administering injections, collecting specimens, conducting point-of-care testing, and completing other duties within scope of practice<br />\r\n\t&nbsp;</li>\r\n\t<li>Accurately documenting patient information, test results, and provider instructions within the electronic medical record to support continuity of care<br />\r\n\t&nbsp;</li>\r\n\t<li>Coordinating patient flow by preparing exam rooms, maintaining supplies, and helping ensure appointments run efficiently<br />\r\n\t&nbsp;</li>\r",
